    - cli_input_boundary  # e196
    - fold_audit_2026_06_03  # e196
    isbefore: []  # e196
    duplicate_of: []  # e196
    not_duplicate_of: []  # e196
    pr_ref:  # e196
    description: "## Origin\n\nMaterialized 2026-06-04 from the 2026-06-03 fold-audit (`~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_06022026_2100_fold_audit_passes_21-40.md`, Family D). Consolidates F40.B1 + F40.B4 previously folded onto INV-sozop. Full evidence remains on INV-sozop's pass-40 discussion entry; this row provides discrete representation as a structurally-distinct failure mode.\n\nThe audit's verdict: F40.B1 is structurally distinct from INV-sozop's \"unhandled Python traceback on malformed/wrong-type input\" scope — INV-sozop is about MALFORMED inputs that traceback (the failure is loud). This row is about WRONG-SHAPE inputs that produce silent rc=0 false success — the failure is invisible. Different downstream consequence (the wrong-traceback handler doesn't fix this), so different fix-site even if both end up at the same `_open_or_die` helper eventually.\n\n## Symptom\n\nSix read-subcommands accept inputs that are valid JSON dicts but lack the required behavior-map schema (no `schema_version`, no `nodes` key). They produce rc=0 with `\"No X found\"` output rather than rejecting the input.\n\nPass-40 6×5 input-shape matrix on /tmp/p40_wrong_schema.json (`{foo: \"bar\"}`):\n\n|  | missing | empty (1B newline) | wrong_schema | array `[1,2,3]` | null_nodes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| search | clean rc=1 | traceback | **rc=0 \"No symbols\"** | traceback | traceback |\n| slice | clean rc=1 | traceback | **rc=1 \"No symbol main\"** | traceback | traceback |\n| explain | clean rc=1 | traceback | **rc=1 \"No symbol main\"** | traceback | traceback |\n| dead-code-maybe | clean rc=1 | traceback | **rc=0 \"No prod fns\"** | traceback | traceback |\n| symbols | clean rc=1 | traceback | **rc=0 cached/empty** | traceback | traceback |\n| routes | clean rc=1 | traceback | **rc=0 cached/empty** | traceback | traceback |\n\n**F40.B1 mechanism:** Each read-subcommand calls `behavior_map.get('nodes', [])`. For `{foo: \"bar\"}`, the dict IS valid (just no `'nodes'` key), so `.get` returns `[]`. Subcommand iterates the empty list and emits `\"No X found\"`. This conflates two distinct conditions:\n\n- (a) **Valid behavior map with no matches** — legitimate empty result.\n- (b) **Input is not a behavior map at all** — input validation failure.\n\n4 of 6 subcommands exit rc=0 in case (b) (search, dead-code-maybe, symbols, routes). The other 2 return rc=1 only because their `--entry` positional fails to find a match in the empty result — the input-shape problem stays invisible there too.\n\n**F40.B4 (parallel boundary):** symbols/routes additionally emit a cache-status footer `\"Using 1 cached / [cached] /tmp/p40_wrong_schema.json / Output: stdout\"` on wrong-schema input. The `\"Using 1 cached\"` line treats the input file as a cached behavior map — the cache-resolver layer has the SAME trust-input-shape assumption as the subcommand-iteration layer. Schema validation needed at TWO sites.\n\n**F40.B2 contrast (NULL finding, motivating fix-path):** missing-file is the ONLY uniformly-handled shape — 6/6 produce identical `\"Error: Input file not found: /path\"` with rc=1 and zero tracebacks. A clean handler exists but is path-only; doesn't extend to content validation. The schema-validation should hoist into the same `_open_or_die` helper.\n\n## Invariant\n\nEvery read-subcommand that accepts `--input` (or auto-discovers via cache resolver) must validate that the loaded content carries `schema_version` and `nodes`/`edges` keys before fan-out. Inputs lacking these keys produce rc=2 with a clear `\"Error: input is not a behavior map (missing schema_version or nodes key)\"` message, NOT rc=0 with `\"No X found\"`.\n\n## Fix sketch\n\nHoist input-shape validation into the shared `_open_or_die` helper (or equivalent): after JSON parse succeeds, verify `schema_version in parsed AND 'nodes' in parsed`. Reject with rc=2 + clear message if either fails. Apply the same check at the cache-resolver layer (F40.B4 sites — currently no schema check at cache-resolver, even when the loaded file is auto-discovered).\n\nThis is a different fix from INV-sozop's exception-handler scope: INV-sozop wants tracebacks to become friendly errors; this row wants silent-rc=0 to become explicit rc=2. Both could land at the same helper but the validation logic is additive, not subsumed.\n\n## Source provenance\n\n- **F40.B1 + F40.B4** — INV-sozop discussion entry 2026-06-03T00:12:28 (pass-40 batch; full 6×5 matrix; paragraphs labeled F40.B1 and F40.B4).\n- F40.B3 (empty-file tracebacks — GENUINE_EXTENSION of INV-sozop per audit; stays on INV-sozop).\n- F40.B2 (missing-file clean handler — NULL finding; stays on INV-sozop as positive evidence).\n\nLab notebook: pass 40 under `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/`.\n\n## Related rows\n\n- Parent: **WI-himas** (META: Add top-level CLI exception handler) — umbrella for all CLI input-boundary failure modes.\n- Sibling: **INV-sozop** (read subcommands traceback on malformed input — the unhandled-exception mode at the same boundary; this row is the silent-success mode).\n- Sibling: **WI-verify-claims-yaml-shape-validation** (Family D — same input-shape-validation gap on a different subcommand).\n- Sibling: **WI-search-pattern-empty-undocumented** (Family D — adjacent input-boundary edge case, documentation-only)."  # e196
    fields: {}  # e196
