  message: "DONE — PR #538 (selfh/dev 8711a6c935). load_substrate rejects a dict lacking the structural 'nodes' key with a typed SubstrateError -> rc=2, instead of the consumer doing data.get('nodes',[]) -> empty -> silent rc=0 'No X found'. BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (live): 'symbols --input noshape.json' (a dict with schema_version but no nodes) -> rc=2, stderr 'Error: ...: not a hypergumbo behavior map — missing required key(s): nodes' (WAS: rc=0 'No symbols found'). Reconciliation note: WI-jukah listed schema_version+nodes as required keys, but co-bundled WI-marul governs schema_version as a warn-first signal, so 'nodes' is the hard-required structural discriminator (the silent-empty root cause) and schema_version warns. Core 100% coverage."  # b19f
